<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Privacy — GIFKI</title>
<meta name="description" content="What GIFKI stores, what it never uploads, and how to delete your account.">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#0f1115">
<style>
:root{--bg:#0f1115;--panel:#181b22;--panel2:#20242e;--line:#2c313c;--text:#e6e9ef;--muted:#96a0b5;--accent:#4c8dff}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);font:16px/1.65 system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",sans-serif}
.wrap{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:30px 20px 60px}
a{color:var(--accent)}
.top{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:26px}
.mark{width:34px;height:34px}
.mark .film{fill:var(--panel2);stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:2}
.mark .holes rect{fill:var(--accent);opacity:.55}
.mark .cel{fill:var(--accent)}
.name{font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;font-size:18px}
h1{font-size:28px;margin:0 0 6px}
.sub{color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 26px;font-size:14px}
h2{font-size:17px;margin:28px 0 8px}
p,li{color:#d4d9e4}
.card{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:16px 18px;margin:18px 0}
.card.good{border-color:#2c5e45;background:#162219}
.card.good h2{margin-top:0}
ul{padding-left:20px;margin:8px 0}
footer{margin-top:40px;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;
  display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}
footer .grow{flex:1}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="top">
    <svg class="mark" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true">
      <rect x="1" y="9" width="62" height="46" rx="7" class="film"/>
      <g class="holes">
        <rect x="6" y="15" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="6" y="28" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="6" y="41" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/>
        <rect x="51" y="15" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="51" y="28" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="51" y="41" width="7" height="7" rx="2"/>
      </g>
      <rect class="cel" x="19" y="19" width="26" height="26" rx="4"/>
    </svg>
    <span class="name">GIFKI</span>
  </div>

  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="sub">Last updated 21 October 2026</p>

  <div class="card good">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>Your drawings never leave your device. GIFKI runs entirely inside your browser, there are no adverts, no analytics and no tracking, and the only thing ever sent anywhere is your email address when you choose to sign in.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Your drawings and projects</h2>
  <p>Everything you draw stays in your own browser. Frames, layers and saved projects are kept in your browser's storage on your device. They are never uploaded to us or to anyone else.</p>
  <p>When you export a GIF, PNG, sprite sheet, ZIP, video or project file, it is made inside your browser and saved straight to your device. Nothing passes through a server.</p>
  <p>Because the work lives in your browser, clearing your browsing data or using a private window will remove it. Use <b>Save project</b> to keep a copy as a file.</p>

  <h2>Signing in</h2>
  <p>Signing in is optional. GIFKI works as a guest.</p>
  <p>If you do sign in, this happens:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>You type your email address, and a six digit code is emailed to you. The email is sent through Google Apps Script using a Gmail account owned by Kiaan Ganesh Shetty.</li>
    <li>Your email address and the display name you choose are stored by that script so it can recognise you next time.</li>
    <li>The code itself is never stored in readable form, works for ten minutes, and can only be used once.</li>
    <li>Your browser keeps a sign-in token for 30 days so you do not have to sign in again. Signing out removes it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Your email address is used only to send sign-in codes and to keep your profile. It is never sold, shared or used for marketing.</p>

  <h2>Guests</h2>
  <p>Guests have no account. The export count is a number kept in your own browser, not on a server.</p>

  <h2>What GIFKI does not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No analytics, no tracking pixels and no advertising.</li>
    <li>No third-party scripts. The page loads no code from anywhere else.</li>
    <li>No cookies used to follow you around.</li>
    <li>No selling or sharing of personal information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Other companies involved</h2>
  <p>The site itself is hosted by Render, which like any web host records ordinary request information such as IP addresses in its server logs. Sign-in emails are delivered by Google. Those companies handle that data under their own privacy policies.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>GIFKI is suitable for all ages. The only personal information it can collect is an email address, and only if someone chooses to sign in.</p>

  <h2>Deleting your information</h2>
  <p>Signing out clears the sign-in details from your browser. To have your stored email address and display name deleted, email <a href="mailto:gshetty1978@gmail.com">gshetty1978@gmail.com</a> and say which address to remove.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:gshetty1978@gmail.com">gshetty1978@gmail.com</a>.</p>

  <footer>
    <span>GIFKI — A Kiaan Ganesh Shetty Creation</span>
    <span class="grow"></span>
    <a href="/">Open GIFKI</a>
    <a href="/copyright.gifki">Copyright</a>
  </footer>
</div>
</body>
</html>
